In `MoeFCGemm::run_kernel_` (`cpp/tensorrt_llm/cutlass_extensions/include/cutlass_extensions/gemm/kernel/moe_cutlass_kernel.h`, current main):

```cpp
typename Mma::IteratorA iterator_A(
    LayoutA(ldm_A), ptr_A, {problem_size.m(), problem_size.k()}, thread_idx, tb_offset_A);
```

`LayoutA(ldm_A)` turns into a temporary `IteratorA::Params` that is destroyed at the end of the statement, but `PredicatedTileAccessIterator` keeps `Params const &params_`, so every later `++iterator_A` / `add_tile_offset` reads a dead object. Same for `iterator_B`, and for the scale iterator built with `initialize_scale(LayoutScaleZero(ldm_Scale), ...)` in the dq path.

With nvcc the stack bytes happen to survive and it works. With clang at -O2/-O3 the loads from the dead object are treated as undefined and most of the cp.async copies that load A and B read from garbage addresses. We hit it through FlashInfer's copy of this file: `CUDA_ERROR_ILLEGAL_ADDRESS` on the first bf16 `cutlass_fused_moe` call (DeepSeek-V2-Lite shapes, sm_121a), and compute-sanitizer reports invalid 16-byte global reads in `MoeFCGemm<MmaMultistage<GemmShape<32,128,64>, ...>>`. In clang's PTX for `moe_gemm_kernels_bf16_bf16.cu`, 2370 of the 2520 `cp.async` copies (in all 75 kernels that use `cp.async`) take their source address from a register that is never written, at -O2 and at -O3; at -O1, none do. With the change below, none do at -O3.

Giving the Params a name removes the illegal address for us (compute-sanitizer memcheck on the same call: 1356 errors before, every one it printed an invalid 16-byte global read; no memory errors after):

```cpp
typename Mma::IteratorA::Params params_A{LayoutA(ldm_A)};  // braces: with parens this declares a function
typename Mma::IteratorA iterator_A(
    params_A, ptr_A, {problem_size.m(), problem_size.k()}, thread_idx, tb_offset_A);
typename Mma::IteratorB::Params params_B{LayoutB(ldm_B)};
typename Mma::IteratorB iterator_B(
    params_B, ptr_B, {problem_size.k() * kInterleave, problem_size.n() / kInterleave}, thread_idx, tb_offset_B);
// dq path
typename Mma::IteratorScale::Params params_scale{LayoutScaleZero(ldm_Scale)};
```

